# An async iteration over an array, a Map, a Set or a typed array steps as the sync iteration does and stands for the wrapper the language puts around the sync iterator, which is never made:
# each value, also the one of the last step, is awaited with one turn of the job queue more than an await takes; what a step throws arrives one turn later; a close takes one turn.
# The prototypes of these classes are closed for @@asyncIterator, so only the object itself can have one: its names are proven or tested, and the protocol asks where the test fails.
# A generator keeps its wrapper, because the wrapper closes it one turn before the loop hears of a value that rejects.
# In an async generator no await takes a turn more: a second await takes that turn. The iterator of such an arm does nothing with what `next` is given, so a value that is sent changes nothing
# FORM: Prepared optimizing
# RUN: pass ExpandIteration
# RUN(ABSENT): pass ExpandIteration
# RUN(AWAITS): pass ExpandIteration
# RUN(TURNS): pass ExpandIteration
# RUN(PROVEN): pass ExpandProvenIterations ExpandIteration
# RUN(LEFT): pass ExpandIteration
# STATISTIC: IterationsExpandedByClass = 12
# STATISTIC: IterationsExpandedGenerically = 2
# CHECK: outcome: Changed
# An arm that awaits has a close with an effect, so it waits for the pass that expands everything.
# PROVEN: outcome: Unchanged
# PROVEN-NEXT: outcome: Changed

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
layout L0 kind=Instance name="Backwards" constructor=f12 flags=[HasHeritage] flow={baseState=BuiltinClass baseClass=Array impossibleMutations=[ChangePrototype] addedKeysAreComplete=true} classFlow={evaluations=AtMostOnce prototypeLink=Fixed staticLink=Fixed prototypeNamesAreComplete=true staticNamesAreComplete=true namedMembers=[{key=@@iterator function=f13 mutability=Fixed}]}

